lots.description:
The provider will be responsible for delivering a comprehensive Lung Cancer Screening Programme across the SWAG Cancer Alliance region.
The scope of the service includes, but is not limited to:
• identification, engagement and recruitment of eligible participants;
• delivery of lung cancer screening assessments and associated clinical activity;
• provision of low-dose computed tomography (LDCT) scanning services;
• management of participant pathways, including referrals, follow-up activity and communication of outcomes;
• provision of all staffing, equipment, facilities, information systems and operational support required to deliver the service;
• collection and reporting of activity, performance and quality data; and
• delivery of interventions designed to maximise participation, improve accessibility and reduce health inequalities.
Services must be delivered in accordance with all applicable legislation, NHS policies, national Lung Cancer Screening Programme requirements, quality standards, information governance requirements and contractual obligations.
Full details of the service requirements are contained within the Invitation to Tender documentation.
